{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012xsKAf29BQRCQoD19x9fFY","type":"tool_result","content":"=== K8s prose check (non-source-tag) ===\n=== lowercase pod ===\n53:3. `kubectl top pods` returns an error on a cluster whose Pods are all `Running` and healthy. What is the most likely cause, and what is the general pattern it belongs to?\n816:**Eviction.** \"If a pod is evicted from the node, all corresponding containers are also evicted, along with their logs\" [source: k8s-docs-logging-architecture-2026-08-23]. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §4 — pods that start and then don't stay]* The Pod that got OOMKilled and evicted at 3 a.m. took the evidence with it.\n=== OTel line 300-303 ===\n                          ▼\n              ┌───────────────────────┐\n              │  OTel COLLECTOR       │\n              │  receive · process ·  │\n=== SRE line 139 ===\nMonitoring, in its canonical definition, is \"collecting, processing, aggregating, and displaying real-time quantitative data about a system\" [source: sre-book-monitoring-definitions-2026-08-31]. Notice what that sentence assumes: somebody already decided *which* quantitative data. Google's own SRE text lists four reasons to monitor, and every one of them is a question chosen in advance [source: sre-book-monitoring-definitions-2026-08-31]:\n=== pattern phrase in ch18 ===\n72:s the pattern *an object without its component does nothing\n360: top` side: ***an object without its component does nothing\n437: pattern:** ***an object without its component does nothing","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca767-6404-4917-ae73-7379181f9d4c","uuid":"ccf5b5ba-196a-4164-a6f5-2d9493d38109","timestamp":"2026-08-31T21:57:52.736Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== K8s prose check (non-source-tag) ===\n=== lowercase pod ===\n53:3. `kubectl top pods` returns an error on a cluster whose Pods are all `Running` and healthy. What is the most likely cause, and what is the general pattern it belongs to?\n816:**Eviction.** \"If a pod is evicted from the node, all corresponding containers are also evicted, along with their logs\" [source: k8s-docs-logging-architecture-2026-08-23]. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §4 — pods that start and then don't stay]* The Pod that got OOMKilled and evicted at 3 a.m. took the evidence with it.\n=== OTel line 300-303 ===\n                          ▼\n              ┌───────────────────────┐\n              │  OTel COLLECTOR       │\n              │  receive · process ·  │\n=== SRE line 139 ===\nMonitoring, in its canonical definition, is \"collecting, processing, aggregating, and displaying real-time quantitative data about a system\" [source: sre-book-monitoring-definitions-2026-08-31]. Notice what that sentence assumes: somebody already decided *which* quantitative data. Google's own SRE text lists four reasons to monitor, and every one of them is a question chosen in advance [source: sre-book-monitoring-definitions-2026-08-31]:\n=== pattern phrase in ch18 ===\n72:s the pattern *an object without its component does nothing\n360: top` side: ***an object without its component does nothing\n437: pattern:** ***an object without its component does nothing","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
