{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNYvX1rhw1kJe7VZxFEzee","type":"tool_result","content":"580:| 72 | Expecting `kubectl top` to work without metrics-server. | `kubectl top` and autoscaling depend on the **resource metrics pipeline** (metrics-server) collecting from kubelets. | [source] |\n607:| 89 | Naming three OpenTelemetry signals. | There are **four**: traces, metrics, logs, and **Baggage** (contextual information passed between signals). Baggage is the one candidates drop. | [source] |\n608:| 90 | Confusing **span** with **trace**. | A span is one unit of work. A trace is the whole request path, made of one or more spans, beginning with a **root span**. | [source] |\n609:| 91 | \"Logs are the richest observability signal.\" | Logs typically **lack contextual information** and are \"not extremely useful for tracking code execution on their own\"; they become useful inside a span or correlated with a trace. | [source] |\n610:| 92 | Confusing **SLI** with **SLO**. | SLI = the **measurement** of service behavior, ideally from the user's perspective. SLO = the **objective**, how reliability is communicated by attaching SLIs to business value. | [source] |\n611:| 93 | \"Prometheus pushes metrics.\" | Prometheus **pulls** (scrapes) over HTTP. Pushing is supported only via the **Pushgateway** intermediary, for short-lived jobs. | [source] |\n612:| 94 | \"Prometheus is a good billing system.\" | Explicitly not: if you need 100% accuracy, such as per-request billing, Prometheus is the wrong choice — it trades completeness for reliability. | [source] |\n613:| 95 | \"Prometheus needs distributed storage / clustered backends.\" | Each server is **standalone and autonomous**, deliberately, so it works when the rest of your infrastructure is broken. | [source] |\n614:| 96 | \"Prometheus was the first CNCF project.\" | Kubernetes was first; Prometheus was the **second**, joining in 2016. | [source] |\n618:| 100 | \"A service mesh requires changing application code.\" | The defining property is delivering zero-trust security, observability, and traffic management **without code changes**. | [source] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eedca767-6404-4917-ae73-7379181f9d4c","uuid":"c4cff5fc-48db-4087-8356-ad500ee5e87c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T21:59:17.870Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"580:| 72 | Expecting `kubectl top` to work without metrics-server. | `kubectl top` and autoscaling depend on the **resource metrics pipeline** (metrics-server) collecting from kubelets. | [source] |\n607:| 89 | Naming three OpenTelemetry signals. | There are **four**: traces, metrics, logs, and **Baggage** (contextual information passed between signals). Baggage is the one candidates drop. | [source] |\n608:| 90 | Confusing **span** with **trace**. | A span is one unit of work. A trace is the whole request path, made of one or more spans, beginning with a **root span**. | [source] |\n609:| 91 | \"Logs are the richest observability signal.\" | Logs typically **lack contextual information** and are \"not extremely useful for tracking code execution on their own\"; they become useful inside a span or correlated with a trace. | [source] |\n610:| 92 | Confusing **SLI** with **SLO**. | SLI = the **measurement** of service behavior, ideally from the user's perspective. SLO = the **objective**, how reliability is communicated by attaching SLIs to business value. | [source] |\n611:| 93 | \"Prometheus pushes metrics.\" | Prometheus **pulls** (scrapes) over HTTP. Pushing is supported only via the **Pushgateway** intermediary, for short-lived jobs. | [source] |\n612:| 94 | \"Prometheus is a good billing system.\" | Explicitly not: if you need 100% accuracy, such as per-request billing, Prometheus is the wrong choice — it trades completeness for reliability. | [source] |\n613:| 95 | \"Prometheus needs distributed storage / clustered backends.\" | Each server is **standalone and autonomous**, deliberately, so it works when the rest of your infrastructure is broken. | [source] |\n614:| 96 | \"Prometheus was the first CNCF project.\" | Kubernetes was first; Prometheus was the **second**, joining in 2016. | [source] |\n618:| 100 | \"A service mesh requires changing application code.\" | The defining property is delivering zero-trust security, observability, and traffic management **without code changes**. | [source] |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
